# The HMAC keys the bridge verifies the portal Worker's signature with: {"<key_id>": "<key>"}.
# 1Password item "Milkshake Farm Command HMAC" (DeLoSecrets), by UUID, field keys_json. The same
# item feeds Milkshake's milkshake-farm-consumer (MILKSHAKE_FARM_COMMAND_KEYS) and the Worker's
# MILKSHAKE_COMMAND_HMAC_KEY (field hmac_key).
FARM_COMMAND_KEYS="op://DeLoSecrets/gjiz7doxfjzvv3oldeob24yafq/keys_json"

# Mercury webhook endpoints (Milkshake Story 9.6, docs/farm-commands.md 16.3.1 and 16.14 step 6).
# Left unset until `ms mercury webhook register --apply` prints the endpoint id and the op://
# reference of the item it created; then, references only:
#   MERCURY_WEBHOOK_ENDPOINT_1=<endpoint id, a plain uuid, not a secret>
#   MERCURY_WEBHOOK_SECRET_1="op://DeLoSecrets/<item-uuid>/credential"
# _2 exists only during a rotation (register --rotate). FARM_COMMAND_KEYS above must also hold a
# mercury-hook-<yyyy-mm> key: the route signs its hook requests with the greatest such key id.
